  "caption": "Quinn is 24 and wakes up stiff as a rusty robot every morning. It takes about an hour to loosen up, a walk helps, and resting on the couch somehow makes it worse.\n\nBack pain in young adults that eases with movement and worsens with rest may be inflammatory rather than mechanical, and it is often picked up late.\n\nWhat can help: note how long morning stiffness lasts, track whether exercise helps and rest hurts, tell your GP about night pain and any eye, skin or bowel symptoms, keep exercising, and ask about a rheumatology review if the pattern persists.\n\nGet it checked if you have a painful red eye that keeps returning, psoriasis, bowel changes or swelling in other joints.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
